# Lana Del Rey shares Thanksgiving update on incoming new albums: “It feels meant to be – it makes me wonder where I would even go after this”

> 🎵 *Curated Music Story from NME Music Official Publications*

### 📖 The Full Story

Music News Lana Del Rey shares Thanksgiving update on incoming new albums: “It feels meant to be – it makes me wonder where I would even go after this” She also said she was "close to wrapping up, although they did take so many unexpected turns over the years” By Liberty Dunworth | 27th November 2026 Lana Del Rey live at Reading 2024. Credit: Andy Ford for NME

Lana Del Rey has shared a message with fans celebrating Thanksgiving, and giving an update on when to expect her new albums.

The singer has been hinting at a new album and the follow up to 2023’s ‘ Did You Know That There’s a Tunnel Under Ocean Blvd ’ for years now. In January 2024 she said that the work on the record began in 2021 and that it would be her first full-length foray into country music.

### 🎤 Key Highlights & Community Reactions

No official release date has been announced, and Del Rey has also said that there is another, untitled companion album on the way too – explaining that it came together as “so much has happened over the last four years, so much time waiting for things to come together”.

Now, in a new post celebrating Thanksgiving, the ‘Video Games’ singer has shared her gratitude for her fans, and shared an update on when she might drop the highly anticipated LPs.

“The albums are coming along so well. I’m happy with them. Taking time cooking but definitely gonna be out at the perfect time considering how much music is on both of them,” she explained on Instagram. “Definitely getting close to wrapping up although it did take so many unexpected turns over the years. Can’t say I saw it coming but what came out of it feels meant to be – it makes me wonder where I would even go after this.”

She added that one release she has planned called ‘You’ve Got A Friend’ has “lyrically so much going over what happened in the last three years”, although didn’t explain whether the title was for a song or for one of the albums.

She added that it would explore how there is “no way that the things that happen could be random”, and reassured fans that she was still working hard to get the new music to them as soon as possible.

